# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# This file is read by Pages itself and is not served as an asset. It only has an
# effect on a Pages deployment — every other host ignores it, so it is safe to
# keep in the repository and in the bundle `tools/deploy-pages.mjs` stages.
#
# It covers the files Pages answers itself, which are `robots.txt` and
# `sitemap.xml`: everything else readers ask for is relayed by `_worker.js` from
# the CMS, and arrives with the headers the CMS set. Two rules that used to live
# here are gone for that reason — `/admin` (a redirect to the CMS now, which
# serves its own noindex) and `/assets/fonts/*` (relayed from the CMS under
# `/_instatic/`, hashed and immutable already).
#
# Note how it is written: when several rules match one request, Pages *merges*
# their headers, and a header set twice is joined with a comma rather than
# overridden. So give each header to each path exactly once.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
